## Experiment setup

**Qwen3-8B** (teacher, thinking disabled) is distilled into **Qwen3-0.6B-Base** (student) on
the MATH500 train split (7.5k problems). Rollouts are sampled at temperature 1.0 and capped
at 1024 tokens. The loss is reverse KL against the teacher over every completion token.

Optimization is 1 epoch (234 steps) at lr 2e-5, 32 prompts per step, in bf16. Evaluation
runs every 25 steps on 100 fixed MATH500 problems with 8 samples each — tracking avg@8 and
pass@8 — plus reverse KL on a held-out set of prompts.


## Results

All values are percentages, 8 samples per problem. The micro-average pools all 1,547
problems; bold marks the better of the two methods.

**Table 1.** OPD vs. SKD across six math benchmarks.

